      "start_seconds": 274.8,
      "end_seconds": 305.46,
      "duration_seconds": 30.66,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. It's hard to say. Perimenopause is one possibility and a thyroid problem another, and I'd rather not commit yet. I think a blood count makes sense here, for irregular periods. The treatment will be estradiol gel, 1 pump, once a day, long term. That should help with menopausal symptoms. Regular exercise, light layers and avoiding triggers can help."
